    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>
[[ if test='valx=valx_1' ]]
<br> For the function \(f(x)=\log (x), \) the domain of \(f(x)\) is \(x>0, \) thus \(x={@valx@}\) is the vertical asymptote. \(f({@valx@})=\log ({@valx@})\) which is undefined. 

[[ else ]]
<br> For the function \(f(x)=\log (x), \) the domain of \(f(x)\) is \({@ta_2@}, \) thus, the value of the function \(f({@valx@})={@val_valx_2@} = {@val_2@}\) which  is well-defined. 
[[/ if]]
</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
